 kubernetes cluster running  our tensor role model to do the  predictions and these predictions are at  a file level and once they are  classified they are now stored once  again into cloud storage this is what  the prediction for that area looks like  and as we can see every single pixel has  a value for one out of ten possible  classes as these land-cover files are  written into cloud storage those trigger  another cloud function that tells our  server to upload that image back into  Earth engine where it gets stored into  an image collection which contains the  land cover maps for the entire world for  all the years that we have extracted now  these land cover maps are very useful  for decision makers and other  organizations to make more informed  decisions about what what resources are  in the earth and every pixel tells a  story especially when we see the change  now one of the very cool things about  Earth engine is that once the data is in  Earth engine it's not only visible  within Earth engine but it's also  accessible to other external  applications which made it possible for  us to build a custom web application  using angularjs and Maps API to request  both the land cover images and the  Landsat images and then render them into  our application so let's take a look at  some locations here we are in Cambodia  what we can see here is the dark green  that's forest and all that amber  yellowish think that's farmland and if  you pay attention to the central region  of that forest we turn  the animation from 2013 to 2018 we can  see how that farmland is slowly eating  through this protected land land cover  makes it easier to quantify but if we  choose the Landsat images then we can  clearly see how this is affecting some  very important habitats in Cambodia now  we can also check this now we can go  into the amazons this is Peru and we see  this thing that looks kind of like bad  River that is going down and if we turn  the animation on then we'll see a very  interesting thing that this is growing  and kind of flowing as if a new river  was going was being created well this is  not actually a river this is toxic waste  and heavy metal residues coming from a  mine nearby fortunately some researchers  in Peru are looking at some trees and  plant species that can grow in these  hazardous environments to help clean up  the area and now if we go all the way to  Iran  this is Lake Urmia the largest lake in  Iran and we can see how the water level  is decreasing and this is due to the  construction of dams and the effects of  global warming in fact that little green  patch that we see in nearby the water  that used to be an island surrounded by  water so as we can see these land cover  maps tell us a story and have a lot of  very insightful information about the  regions that help us quantify what's  happening in there but they take a lot  of time and effort to create these in  fact to create a map of entire USA it  takes at least five years to create one  of these so we try generating the maps  for the entire United States and we  managed to get the maps  from 2013 to 2018 in under 24 hours so  let me show you a quote from Mahatma  Gandhi what we're doing to the forests  in the world is but a mirror reflection  of what we are doing to ourselves and to  one another but it's not all bad news  there's also a bunch of very cool  efforts that are happening around the  world something's not working there we  go  so for example this is the great green  wall project that is happening in Africa  this is in conjunction with a bunch of  different countries and communities  working together to plant a lot of trees  and edible plants to create a division  between the now growing Sahara Desert  and protect the forests in Africa and  there are also some reforestation  efforts going in amel in the Amazon  where people are gathering seeds from  the forests around them and then mixing  them with soil and planting in affected  areas here we can see how the these  plants look like after 3 to 6 months of  growing and then these trees after 5 to  7 years of growing we all share the same  planet and every little action like  using less plastic or growing your own  food will have an impact and you like  this project or see or would like to see  how it was created you can follow this  link and it will take you to our github  repo or you can share the story in  medium thank you  [Applause]  [Music]

